2026-09-11T17:30:00.000Z note GO-4 completed at the gate. The implement report took the disk half and refused the wall-time half rather than presenting an incremental install as a cold one, which was right. Taken here on manifests-only copies of ce84a37 and the merge commit, each installed with --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts into its OWN empty --store-dir, so both rows are genuinely cold: before 145 packages / 172 lockfile resolutions / node_modules 128 MB / store 127 MB / 5.1 s; after 203 (+58) / 251 (+79) / 179 MB (+40%) / 177 MB (+50 MB) / 10.4 s. The cold-store install DOUBLES, x2.04, and that is the number R-1 asked for. Ten seconds is not a threat to M6's 30-minute budget, so R-1 is answered rather than carried. Stated rather than implied: the metadata cache was warm and the link fast, so a genuine first-ever install on a slow connection scales with the extra 50 MB of download and not with the 5.3 s. The implementer's own figures (143 -> 200 packages, 128 -> 192 MB) differ because that pair was the real workspace with sources present and scripts enabled; direction and magnitude agree and neither is transcribed from the other.
